Package: ggvmap
Title: Voronoi Map Treemaps for ggplot2
Version: 0.3.0.9000
Authors@R: c(
    person("Loukas", "Theodosiou", email = "loukesio@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Franck", "Lebeau", role = "cph",
           comment = "Author of d3-voronoi-map, whose iteration heuristics are ported in the layout solver; see inst/COPYRIGHTS"))
Description: Compute and visualise Voronoi map treemaps -- space-filling
    partitions of polygons where each cell's area is proportional to
    an underlying weight. The algorithm iteratively adapts site positions and
    power-diagram weights until convergence, following the approach of Nocaj
    and Brandes (2012) <doi:10.1111/j.1467-8659.2012.03078.x> with the
    iteration heuristics of the 'd3-voronoi-map' JavaScript library, and
    fits layouts those heuristics cannot with a damped Newton method
    (Kitagawa, Merigot and Thibert 2019 <doi:10.4171/JEMS/889>). Supports
    hierarchical (grouped) layouts, a decorative outer annotation ring, and
    flag / image / value annotations. A pure R solver for convex layouts
    with first-class ggplot2 integration.
    An optional 'polyclip' backend supports non-convex regions, holes and
    disconnected pieces, with optional 'sf' input for projected map boundaries.
